{
  "_doc": "CU-VALENCE REGISTRY (user-directed 2026-07-04). Maps a specific policy TARGET (+ action direction) to its valence FOR CREDIT UNIONS: +1 good, -1 bad, 0 neutral. The stance model reads the member's stance toward the target at 0.915 acc; this registry supplies valence (model's own valence knowledge is only 0.689, esp. weak on pro-CU targets). Two-hop compose(stance, valence) ceiling = 0.872 on the tweet gold. EXTEND THIS: add entries for uncovered high-volume targets (apply_two_hop_stance.py --uncovered surfaces them ranked). Each entry: match=keywords (lowercase, any-hit), dir=optional {rein_in:+/-1 override when reform/oversight/repeal language present}, valence=base.",
  "entries": [
    {"key": "cfpb_expansion", "match": ["cfpb", "consumer financial protection bureau"], "valence": -1, "rein_flips": true, "note": "expanding CFPB power/funding/reach = -1; reform/commission/appropriations-oversight/repeal = +1"},
    {"key": "interchange_cap", "match": ["interchange", "credit card competition act", "cca", "swipe fee", "durbin amendment", "routing mandate"], "valence": -1, "rein_flips": true, "note": "caps/routing mandates = -1; blocking/repealing = +1 (CUs side with banks here)"},
